      "writtenOn": "2023-09-20T17:21:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point, yes, the texture proxy will fail to instantiate later if format is A8 on Dawn. The software path renderer doesn\u0027t need a storage texture but one that can be sampled. It probably makes sense to add a parameter to this function to indicate the storage usage, assuming we want to continue using this pooling scheme here. Alternately we could have each PathAtlas create its textures directly.\n\nAlso, I don\u0027t think there is any usage validation during TextureProxy creation, so this won\u0027t fail right away but later while instantiating the texture. I think it makes sense to validate the usage when creating the TextureInfo that\u0027s used to initialize the proxy.\n\nI\u0027ll send a follow-up that makes those two changes.",
      "parentUuid": "bdec3421_c75b9204",
